From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Feb 27 20:56:36 1997
From: barnwell () jbsvax ! eksystems ! com (Barnwell () eksystems ! com voice 508-303-6905)
Date: Thu, 27 Feb 1997 20:56:36 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: any body got any idea what space there isn't enough of??
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078608810570


I got lots of answers but the Grand Prize (a NO expense paid trip to the EKS 
World Headquarters located in suburan Marlboro Ma.) goes to 

Knut.Hellebo@nho.hydro.com

Who hit the nail on the Head with 

You should check the kernel values for the 'proc' subsystem, ie
'sysconfig -q proc' and check the 'per-proc' values. Probably one of
these get exhausted. Also check for temp space free (/tmp and /var/tmp).
You can get a hint on what the file requires by doing a 'size file'

So I upped the obvious params by alot (double)

  max-proc-per-user 
  per-proc-stack-size 
  max-per-proc-stack-size 
  per-proc-data-size 
  max-per-proc-data-size 
  max-per-proc-address-space 
  per-proc-address-space 

And all was well with the linker

JB

