Cedric

> Anyone knows how to read /usr/adm/binary.errlog file?

You should install DECevent on your system ( its on the operating system
CD's ). Once this is installed do:

dia  -R |more

where -R says to read the file from the latest to oldest


The unsupported method of looking at the binary.errlog is to use

uerf  -R |more

uerf is not able to read the binary.errlog of the new systems ie 4100's
and some 8400's and is being replaced by DECevent.

