Hi,

  I asked about swap space and how to stop my machine from killing
applications due to lack of swap space.

  The answer is to place a symbolic link  to your swap partition as
below:
   
    ln -s /dev/rzxy /sbin/swapdefault

where "xyz" is your swap partition.  In my case, my swap partition is
named /dev/rz0b.

