The original problem was:

> With each attempt to log in, the following message is returned after 
> the password has been accepted:
> 
> Can't rewrite terminal control entry for ttyp1
> 
> Then the session is never established and logs out.  This is a DU 4.0 machine 
> running with C2 security.  I believe the ttys db has been corrupted 
> and have logged an emergency call to Digital.  Has anyone else 
> experienced this situation before?  Any thoughts would be 
> appreciated.

What had occurred  was not a corruption of the ttys db after all.  
Instead the password file turned out to be the culprit.  It had been 
overwritten to a zero length file by user bin, group bin.  After 
restoring the password file from backup tape we were operational 
again.

Although the problem has been solved, I am still interested to hear 
if others have had any similar experiences involving the password 
file and DU 4.0.  If so, please contact me.

Thanks to all for their advice!

Dan

