From tru64-unix-managers  Mon Feb 17 17:36:42 1997
From: "Peter Gross" <pag () probita ! com>
Date: Mon, 17 Feb 1997 17:36:42 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: XDMCP query from PC running eXceed
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078608810338

I solved my problem by using the time-honored Unix way: RTFM-ing. 
Unfortunately I had to purchase the correct FM -- "X Window System 
Administrator's Guide" [O'Reilly]. There were a couple of problems.
1. The default xdm configuration file (for CDE), 
/usr/dt/config/Xconfig.con, has per-user authorization turned on. The 
eXceed configuration to use this set a display class of "HCLpcXserver"
and a key "xdmkey". By clearing those two fields in the XDMCP 
configuration of eXceed, the login screen appeared.
2. eXceed needs to use DU 4.0b's font server to get at the fonts 
needed by CDE. By default the font server is not started.
3. Even when the font server is running, there were complaints about 
missing fonts. It turns out that DU's default font server 
configuration file, /usr/var/X11/fs/config, does not include the CDE 
fonts in the exported catalog! To fix, add /usr/lib/X11/fonts/cde, 
/usr/lib/X11/fonts/cde/75dpi, /usr/lib/X11/fonts/cde/100dpi to the 
catalogue.

Now everything is working quite well.
=======================================
Original Message:
> Hi,
>     We have a new Alphasever 1000 running DU 4.0b. We also have some
> PC's running Hummingbird eXceed X-server software. There are two
> ways to configure eXceed: 1. passive/multi mode, which uses the MS
> Windows window manager to manage the screen, with each Xwindow app
> in its own Windows window; or 2. single/XDMCP query mode, which does
> an XDMCP query to a specified host, and then the X session is in one
> large Windows window. This allows you run native window managers
> like HP Vue, or CDE. Our prior experience with XDMCP query mode was
> on HP servers, where the VUE login screen would come up on the PC,
> the user would then login, and voila, HP VUE desktop. Under DU 4.0,
> eXceed gets and error: xdm session declined. We had configured the
